---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { FileExplorerPlayground } from '../../components/FileExplorerDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="File Explorer"
  description="Browse a folder of read-only files with a tree, tabs, syntax colors, and search across names and text."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">File Explorer</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Reads a repository like a code editor does. Folders come from the paths, files open in tabs with syntax colors, and
    one search box finds file names and the lines that mention a word.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <FileExplorerPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A Soul repository"
      code={`import { FileExplorer } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/file-explorer";

<div className="h-[36rem]">
  <FileExplorer
    label="Soul"
    files={[
      { path: "SOUL.md", content: soulMd },
      { path: "agents/scout/tools.ts", content: toolsTs },
      { path: "assets/map.png", unavailable: "Images cannot be displayed here." },
    ]}
    defaultPath="SOUL.md"
  />
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass a flat list of files. Each path uses <code>/</code> between folders. A file has <code>content</code>, or{' '}
      <code>unavailable</code> with the reason it has no text. The explorer fills its parent, so give the parent a
      height.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Search</h2>
    <p>
      Search ignores case. It lists matching file names, then every matching line grouped by file, with the line number.
      Pick a line to open the file there. The line is marked and every match in the file is highlighted. Search stops
      after 500 lines.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The tree is a <code>tree</code> with one tab stop. Up and Down move, Right opens a folder, Left closes it or goes
      to the parent, Home and End jump, and Enter opens a file. The search summary is a status message. Each open tab
      has a Close button named after the file; middle-click also closes a tab. The file text is a focusable region named
      after its path.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
